-- title:
--   Accepted-exchange and holding contributions to a transition
-- statement:
--   Let $\alpha$ have decidable equality, let $x,c,y\in\alpha$ be the current state, proposed candidate, and target state, and let $a\in\mathbb R$ be an acceptance parameter. Define
--   $$\operatorname{exchangeOutcome}(x,c,y,a)=a\,\mathbf1_{\{c=y\}}+(1-a)\,\mathbf1_{\{x=y\}}.$$
--   The expression combines the accepted move to $c$ with the rejected move staying at $x$. If the candidate equals the current state, both contributions are included at that same state. The definition allows arbitrary real $a$; interpreting its coefficients as probabilities requires the additional condition $0\leq a\leq1$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/meelgroup/counting-matroid/blob/dd16a4628fdb095c58fe0f3dfd8e353c6e97443c/CountingMatroid/Analysis/SelectedMetropolisKernel.lean#L15-L19

